WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.269 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.938
-New year, fresh start.

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:08.741
Couple of resolutions.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:11.177
No more callbacks...

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.879
in "Corrections."

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.980
I want each one
to be self-contained

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:16.716
so people can jump in.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:19.786
They're incentivized
to start watching now.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:23.789
Another one of my resolutions --
get back to the gym.

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:26.425
Took a couple of weeks off.
Made a difference.

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:29.162
Here is a picture
from earlier today.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:33.999
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:35.835
So no more callbacks.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.906
Hey, I was told
my Jennifer Coolidge impression

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:42.608
sounds like my
Owen Wilson impression,

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:44.710
which is deeply wrong

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.680
because Jennifer Coolidge
is like, "Wow!"

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.050
But Owen Wilson is "Wow!"

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.486
It's about the eyes
are either open or like,

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.455
"Wow."

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.090
"Wow!"

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.759
My impression of the two of them

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:03.462
realizing they're wearing the
same sweater at a holiday party.

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:06.165
"Wow!"
"Wow!"

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:08.268
Sounds the same?

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.272
Uh, ooh.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.040
Here. Can we come over there
for a second?

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.875
We did a --
I leaned my head back

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.244
in "A Closer Look" on Monday,

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.613
and a bunch of people noticed
I had a scar on my chin

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:23.916
and asked why I have a scar on
my chin.

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:26.252
Have any of you seen
the movie "Road House"?

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.788
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.957
In the film "Road House,"
Patrick Swayze

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:33.492
plays a bouncer,
the head bouncer,

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:36.428
the kind of guy
who's going to do

00:01:36.428 --> 00:01:38.764
whatever it takes
to win a fight.

00:01:38.764 --> 00:01:40.199
He's going to break the rules.

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:46.305
He's going to put himself
at risk when things get gnarly.

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:50.409
Anyway, when I was 16, I was on
the couch watching that movie

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:51.678
and I leaned over
to get popcorn.

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.379
I rolled over, and I banged this
on the coffee table.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:57.250
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:03.322
That's actually not
how I hurt it.

00:02:03.322 --> 00:02:04.490
The only thing
I'm going to say --

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.259
the only true thing
I'm gonna say about it is

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.660
Shoemaker didn't do it.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:11.097
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:20.039
It's not "pri-mer,"
it's "prim-er."

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:22.775
You're nodding, you know,
because it's British.

00:02:24.743 --> 00:02:27.213
And Amazon "Prim" is when
they bring your package

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.214
[British accent] in a lorry.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.016
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:36.356
You don't mix cocaine
with baking powder.

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:39.892
You mix it with baking soda.

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:42.862
An error I made so many times
they kicked me off the corner.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:45.765
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:49.234
I had a very small part...

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:51.370
got cut...

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.106
from season one of "The Wire."

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:58.844
Where I played a dealer
who got it wrong.

00:02:58.844 --> 00:03:00.980
I was like,
"I'm so sorry, Avon."

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.254
Graphics.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.656
One person we talked about --
we made a very hard graphic

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:16.329
in an effort to show
that they had not...

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:19.364
lost their touch
over a long hiatus.

00:03:19.364 --> 00:03:23.036
And it was an alligator
drinking from a beer helmet

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:25.939
in a golf cart
with a bumper sticker that said,

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:28.374
"My other ride is your mom."

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:29.842
We were very impressed,
but when he pointed out

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.512
that is not on the bumper,

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:35.515
therefore that is not
a bumper sticker.

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:38.151
That seems to me a little...

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:39.819
a little severe.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:43.823
With that said, we also
before the break had

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:46.024
Rudy Giuliani
wearing his shirts as pants

00:03:46.024 --> 00:03:47.292
and his pants as a shirt,

00:03:47.292 --> 00:03:48.694
and people said,
"That's not good."

00:03:48.694 --> 00:03:50.063
And, yeah, I get it.

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:52.598
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:54.133
I don't know what we thought
it would look like,

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.536
but I don't -- I don't know
if that was it.

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.908
You guys,
my goal with "Corrections"

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:05.110
is to make you feel
part of this "Late Night" family

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:08.047
because this is a great place
to work with great people.

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:11.617
And so you guys
being a part of this,

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:14.153
obviously there's a good amount
of inside jokes,

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.623
but I want you to feel like
you're a part of this family.

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:18.023
And one of the best parts
of this family

00:04:18.023 --> 00:04:21.494
is when we sort of gently
tease each other

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.696
and I feel nothing
warms my heart more

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.230
than when I feel
like you guys get that

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:26.732
because one of you --
we mentioned this.

00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:29.736
We showed this picture
of an old Santa Claus

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:32.404
in last "Corrections"
and someone said,

00:04:32.404 --> 00:04:34.373
"Hey, I know
what that looks like.

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:36.976
That looks like Wally in respect
in the workplace."

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:41.581
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:45.117
You guys get it.

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:46.285
So burning Wally is great.

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:48.720
Burning me, on the other hand,
is not cool.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.623
And I was on --

00:04:51.623 --> 00:04:55.360
I use this as a safe place
to share with you

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:58.898
how unsettled I am by the 1980s

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:01.734
McDonald's spokesperson
Mac Tonight.

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.771
And instead of empathizing
with me

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:08.841
and hearing that, many of you
have taken advantage of the P.O.

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:15.414
Box address we have given you
to send me just awful --

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:17.784
awful, haunting...

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:19.852
This showed up in the mail.

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:22.989
That dude.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:25.958
A mug.

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:30.363
And then this note,
which just, again, says,

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:35.033
"Forever yours, love
always and forever, Mac."

00:05:35.033 --> 00:05:39.238
Just again, a serial killer's
note card.

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:42.842
Guys, stop sending me
Mac Tonight stuff.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:45.211
We're going to flash
the P.O. Box one more time.

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:47.313 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:49.181 line:0%
Just so you remember,
if you have it,

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:50.950 line:0%
this is the last place
we want it.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:54.687 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.589 --> 00:05:59.859
Last "Corrections," it turned
out some of the stuff

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:02.561
at the desk was made of candy.

00:06:02.561 --> 00:06:05.932
It was edible.
That was our big reveal.

00:06:05.932 --> 00:06:08.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:14.740
I should note they were courtesy
of our sound mixers.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:15.941
His name is Mike Witzer.

00:06:15.941 --> 00:06:19.211
His mother, Andrea,
does this for a living.

00:06:19.211 --> 00:06:20.346
This is a true thing.

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:25.284 line:0%
She has -- You can go to
www.stylewith.me

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:26.718 line:0%
to see the incredible
work she does.

00:06:26.718 --> 00:06:28.487 line:0%
And I'm going to use her.

00:06:28.487 --> 00:06:30.857
I think I'm going to make
edible versions

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:33.492
of my kids' favorite toys.
And then when they misbehave...

00:06:33.492 --> 00:06:40.866
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.866 --> 00:06:42.702
She can do anything.
I was told she can.

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:44.970
I mean, she can't do like paper,
but she can do like, you know,

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:49.275
anything with, like a shape.
I took a bite of of this.

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:51.210
And based on the reaction,
people thought,

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:53.545
"Oh, my God,
he thought that was candy."

00:06:53.545 --> 00:06:54.947
But it turned out
it was plaster.

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:56.549
It was something worse
than plaster.

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:57.850
It was white chocolate.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.985
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.985 --> 00:07:01.753
Which used to be my nickname.

00:07:01.753 --> 00:07:03.389
That was actually my
character's name on "The Wire."

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:06.826
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.263 --> 00:07:15.167
You guys,
I am a Pittsburgh Steelers fan.

00:07:15.167 --> 00:07:17.870
I live and die
with the Pittsburgh Steelers.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.539
Not something I'm proud of
or I think makes me cool.

00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:26.212
If anything, I would consider it
a sort of design flaw.

00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:29.248
Doesn't make me more interesting
to be around.

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:34.486
If I was ever on a dating show,
it wouldn't be my introduction.

00:07:34.486 --> 00:07:35.821
"Hey, I'm Seth.

00:07:35.821 --> 00:07:39.491
I cry when the Steelers lose
and also when they win."

00:07:39.491 --> 00:07:40.393
I know.

00:07:40.393 --> 00:07:42.361
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:46.466
It sucks. Well, they weren't
having much of a season.

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:50.069
And then they kind of
turned it around.

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:51.637
And not only have things
been going well for them,

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:53.638
but all the teams that need to
lose need to lose,

00:07:53.638 --> 00:07:55.708
and so now a thing that I did
not think was possible --

00:07:55.708 --> 00:07:57.943
it's possible they might
actually make the playoffs.

00:07:57.943 --> 00:07:59.578
Three things need to happen
on Sunday.

00:07:59.578 --> 00:08:01.581
They have to win,

00:08:01.581 --> 00:08:03.415
the Bills have to beat
the Patriots,

00:08:03.415 --> 00:08:06.185
and the Jets have to
beat the Dolphins.

00:08:06.185 --> 00:08:09.789
Now, if you watch this show,
you know

00:08:09.789 --> 00:08:11.958
I'm pretty hard on the Jets.

00:08:11.958 --> 00:08:14.126
[ Laughter ]

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:16.361
And if you're a Buddhist,

00:08:16.361 --> 00:08:20.466
you might have heard
about something called karma.

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:23.635
I'm well aware of how this is
likely going to end.

00:08:23.635 --> 00:08:28.073
You know what I mean?
Like, I need the Jets to win.

00:08:28.073 --> 00:08:31.610
And the thing that really
burns me is

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:36.281
either John or Jim --
I can't remember who --

00:08:36.281 --> 00:08:38.284
I mean, they both,
like, tower above me.

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:39.652
[ Laughter ]

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:41.954
So whenever they talk, I look.
They're always backlit.

00:08:41.954 --> 00:08:45.725
[ Laughter ]

00:08:45.725 --> 00:08:47.426
But I remember one of them
once was like, "You know,

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:48.995
you better be careful."
Oh, so it was Jim.

00:08:48.995 --> 00:08:55.300
[ Laughter ]

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.569
He said,
"You better be careful.

00:08:56.569 --> 00:08:58.203
You know, one of these days
you might need

00:08:58.203 --> 00:09:00.038
the Jets to win."
And I was like,

00:09:00.038 --> 00:09:04.442
"If I ever need to root
for the New York Jets,

00:09:04.442 --> 00:09:07.446
I'll eat my script, Jim."

00:09:07.446 --> 00:09:10.316
[ Laughter ]

00:09:12.618 --> 00:09:13.953
Point being...

00:09:13.953 --> 00:09:18.891
[ Laughter ]

00:09:18.891 --> 00:09:20.826
I really want the Jets to win.

00:09:22.528 --> 00:09:24.597
And Mike's mom
"can" make candy paper.

00:09:24.597 --> 00:09:27.767
[ Laughter ]

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:31.537
She told me it was edible.
But now...

00:09:31.537 --> 00:09:33.539
I think if I swallow it,
I'll die.

00:09:46.685 --> 00:09:51.623
Real pencil? Is it pencil?

00:09:51.623 --> 00:09:54.393
Shoemaker, is it pencil?

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:56.195
Shoemaker!

00:09:56.195 --> 00:09:57.696
Is it pencil?

00:09:57.696 --> 00:10:02.634
Shoemaker, is it pencil?

00:10:02.634 --> 00:10:03.736
Shoemaker!

00:10:03.736 --> 00:10:05.337
[ Laughter ]

00:10:05.337 --> 00:10:07.640
Shoemaker, is it pencil?

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:08.840
-Yes.

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:10.342
-Don't [bleep] talk...

00:10:10.342 --> 00:10:12.878
[ Laughter ]

00:10:12.878 --> 00:10:14.847
...in "Corrections."

00:10:16.948 --> 00:10:18.751
Not pencil, you dummy.

